  "scope": "Whole Federer 3.2.39, pp. 275--276: common Minkowski content and both full-radius contents equal actual Hausdorff mass of every closed genuinely m-rectifiable original W in R^n, for all natural m<=n. Finite mass is derived. Retain empty sources, finite multipoint degree-zero sets, zero ambient dimensions and zero normal blocks.",
  "proof_route": "For positive degree, an opaque same-bound extension and the compact closure of the bounded original parameter domain give an exact compact preimage parametrization. Actual area and continuous Suslin multiplicity identify Jacobian density with image-cost Caratheodory measure on Borel sets. Full Borel-partition and finite-subsum laws give a finite disjoint approximation. Restrict Hausdorff measure to the actual finite compact image before compact source image approximation. Disjoint compact cores and a fine null-face coordinate grid give the finite compact source cover, exact Jacobian sum and nearly full image cost. Independent finite layer laws precede local existence. Finite-list recursion proves compactness; actual characteristic integration gives equal layer and image mass sums and the pointwise tube-count inequality. Positive normalization and a finite common cutoff prove the mixed full-real-radius limit comparison. Earlier 3.2.38 bounds compact images, while 3.2.26 and 3.2.37 bound layers below. Proved finite scalar cancellation removes the single approximation error. Degree zero follows independently from actual counting identities.",
  "original_closed_rectifiable_source": true,
